{"authored" [{"question" "q-19147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨1,4,2\\sqrt{2}⟩$ and $q=⟨1,1,\\sqrt{2}⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p+{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "6abcfc503947c7e93a39d0fa8c2989d2424e31f5e4625b225423804228437b4e" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1+2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,p\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}+{p}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p+{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{9}{5} \\\\  & =9(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =9(\\frac{5}{10}+\\frac{2}{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "6abcfc503947c7e93a39d0fa8c2989d2424e31f5e4625b225423804228437b4e" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1fcb7ef625b594b317187e59a3360275bf90c09e83972bf61a90c30f6b704e2d" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "6abcfc503947c7e93a39d0fa8c2989d2424e31f5e4625b225423804228437b4e" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{29}{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "6abcfc503947c7e93a39d0fa8c2989d2424e31f5e4625b225423804228437b4e" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{27}{10}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "6abcfc503947c7e93a39d0fa8c2989d2424e31f5e4625b225423804228437b4e" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{29}{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "6abcfc503947c7e93a39d0fa8c2989d2424e31f5e4625b225423804228437b4e" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{32}{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "6abcfc503947c7e93a39d0fa8c2989d2424e31f5e4625b225423804228437b4e" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{63}{10}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/state.json" "file_sha256" "6abcfc503947c7e93a39d0fa8c2989d2424e31f5e4625b225423804228437b4e" "basis" 1423 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040236/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-1778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{120}^{∘})=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-1778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u+v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the sum formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v={120}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+{120}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡{120}^{∘}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡{120}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-1778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ec22a625be564740b161a2a66fd3e38dacf46fcd5e1aae79ce3478fd7857aa9"} {"question" "q-1778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-1778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\sqrt{3}}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-1778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-162307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams shows all the $5$th roots of unity?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-162307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Geometrically, the $5$th roots of unity have the following properties:\n\n- all of them lie on the unit circle centered in the origin,\n\n- one of the roots is $1,$ corresponding to the point $(1,0)$ on the complex plane,\n\n- the roots form a regular pentagon (regular $5$-sided polygon).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/assets/bf2edb811442fc770f6f3c119c06bca3c17d30537f1941448ddb6ab0afa3eb8a.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-162307" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ec22a625be564740b161a2a66fd3e38dacf46fcd5e1aae79ce3478fd7857aa9"} {"question" "q-162307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-162307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/assets/3a93f28c1b40170c2fede87cdeb5893cdd07e0a3a7c898a760ecdfb2f156b3c8.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/assets/58013857f5024f78c322059e5ffdbf10943b0479722202c972a51ccda4be3525.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/assets/70c37a408e7c4b8dd9b949735ee5e5a8112bceee0f2b879d26052d664b90d46b.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/assets/923d1a1b87833551ae6c451f15a6b5d8bdd75623e8d5c20e86357894bc24683d.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/assets/bf2edb811442fc770f6f3c119c06bca3c17d30537f1941448ddb6ab0afa3eb8a.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-162307" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/assets/bf2edb811442fc770f6f3c119c06bca3c17d30537f1941448ddb6ab0afa3eb8a.png"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-123765" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=1-4t,\\,\\,\\,y={t}^{2}-1,\\,t\\le 0,\n$$\n\nwhat is the range of $x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-123765" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the range of $x,$ note that $x=1-4t\\ge 1$ for all $t\\le 0.$ \n\nConsequently, the range of $x$ is $x\\ge 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-123765" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ec22a625be564740b161a2a66fd3e38dacf46fcd5e1aae79ce3478fd7857aa9"} {"question" "q-123765" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-123765" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ge -4"] ["math" "x\\ge 0"] ["math" "x\\ge 1"] ["math" "x\\le -2"] ["math" "x\\le 1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-123765" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\ge 1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-114251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+1}{({x}^{2}-4)^{2}-12x-21}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-114251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we plug in $x=-1$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+1}{({x}^{2}-4)^{2}-12x-21} & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{[{x}^{2}+2x+1]}^{′}}{{[({x}^{2}-4)^{2}-12x-21]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{2x+2}{4x({x}^{2}-4)-12} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{x+1}{2x({x}^{2}-4)-6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2x+1}{({x}^{2}-4)^{2}-12x-21} & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{x+1}{2x({x}^{2}-4)-6} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{[x+1]}^{′}}{{[2x({x}^{2}-4)-6]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{1}{6{x}^{2}-8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6(-1)^{2}-8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-114251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ec22a625be564740b161a2a66fd3e38dacf46fcd5e1aae79ce3478fd7857aa9"} {"question" "q-114251" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-114251" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-114251" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-141101" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{5y}{x},\\,x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y={x}^{5}$\n- $y={x}^{10}$\n- $y=5{x}^{4}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-141101" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y={x}^{5},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=5{x}^{4}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{5y}{x} \\\\ 5{x}^{4} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5({x}^{5})}{x} \\\\ 5{x}^{4} & =5{x}^{4}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y={x}^{5}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y={x}^{10},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=10{x}^{9}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{5y}{x} \\\\ 10{x}^{9} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5({x}^{10})}{x} \\\\ 10{x}^{9} & \\overset{?}{=}5{x}^{9} \\\\ 5{x}^{9} & \\ne 0.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y={x}^{10}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=5{x}^{4},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=20{x}^{3}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{5y}{x} \\\\ 20{x}^{3} & \\overset{?}{=}\\frac{5(5{x}^{4})}{x} \\\\ 20{x}^{3} & \\overset{?}{=}25{x}^{3} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 5{x}^{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=5{x}^{4}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-141101" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ec22a625be564740b161a2a66fd3e38dacf46fcd5e1aae79ce3478fd7857aa9"} {"question" "q-141101" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-141101" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-141101" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨1,4,2\\sqrt{2}⟩$ and $q=⟨1,1,\\sqrt{2}⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p+{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1+2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,p\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}+{p}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p+{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{9}{2}+\\frac{9}{5} \\\\  & =9(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{5}) \\\\  & =9(\\frac{5}{10}+\\frac{2}{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ec22a625be564740b161a2a66fd3e38dacf46fcd5e1aae79ce3478fd7857aa9"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{29}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{27}{10}"] ["math" "\\frac{29}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{32}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{63}{10}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-19147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{63}{10}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-130620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the possible values of the constant $x$ given that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ x & -1 & -x\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-130620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ x & -1 & -x\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -x\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ x & -x\\end{aligned}|+8|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ x & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(-x+2)-5(-x-2x)+8(-1-x) \\\\  & =-3x+6+15x-8-8x \\\\  & =4x-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/state.json" "file_sha256" "54f90b1ccc34116f0314811ab977f4637168a9e4dbc8b2af40208034154018a3"} {"question" "q-130620" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8ec22a625be564740b161a2a66fd3e38dacf46fcd5e1aae79ce3478fd7857aa9"} {"question" "q-130620" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054574/sta